From 40afef1f060bd66d2cfb3c294b015e1ca2e7de46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bhavya <bhavyajainkalak@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:27:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Catch swapped photos and one face carrying two identities

Page-wide ELA averages a replaced photo away (the photo is a few percent
of the page), so the tampering module missed the most common card
forgery. The photo frame is now compared with the rest of the card:
ELA error per unit of edge strength, inside over outside. A clear
result sets the floor of the forensics score.

The records check links one number to two names but never one face to
two numbers. Each document portrait is now kept as an SFace embedding
in a local index (no image, expires with the scan) and searched on
every screening. Same face under a different name or birth date raises
FACE_UNDER_OTHER_IDENTITY; same face, same holder, other document is
left alone.

training/eval_portrait_ela.py measures both the old and new check on
the generated set and suggests the alarm level.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
